        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(whatsapp): add listGroupsLive for real-time group directory",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe WhatsApp channel directory adapter only registered `listGroups` (which reads from the config map `channels.whatsapp.groups`) but did **not** register `listGroupsLive`. The CLI (and other consumers) prefer `listGroupsLive` when available, so users who have active WhatsApp group memberships but an empty config-based groups map would see `No groups found.` from `openclaw directory groups list --channel whatsapp`.\n\nFixes #76722\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis PR adds `listWhatsAppDirectoryGroupsLive` that fetches groups from the Baileys socket via `groupFetchAllParticipating()`. The function has two code paths:\n\n1. **Process-local controller** (gateway process): uses the existing `getRegisteredWhatsAppConnectionController()` socket — the fast path when a gateway is running.\n2. **Standalone socket** (CLI process): when no process-local controller exists (e.g. `openclaw directory groups list --channel whatsapp` as a standalone command), opens a temporary Baileys socket using stored auth credentials from disk, fetches group metadata, then closes the socket.\n\nBoth paths fall back gracefully to the config-backed `listWhatsAppDirectoryGroupsFromConfig` on failure.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWhatsApp users who have joined groups but haven't manually configured them in `channels.whatsapp.groups` can now see their real group memberships in the directory — from both the gateway process and the standalone CLI. No config changes required.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test extensions/whatsapp/src/directory-config.test.ts` — 11/11 passed\n- `pnpm tsgo:test` — passed\n- Lint + format — passed\n- Rebased onto `upstream/main` — resolves unrelated CI failures in `check-lint`, `check-test-types`\n\n**Real behavior proof** — Linux, Node 24.13.1, commit `0a7ae017e3`, linked WhatsApp account (phone number redacted).\n\nStandalone CLI `openclaw directory groups list --channel whatsapp`:\n```console\n$ openclaw directory groups list --channel whatsapp\n\nGroups (4)\n┌────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┐\n│ ID                             │ Name                    │\n├────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┤\n│ 120363409866058990@g.us        │ openclaw_test           │\n│ 120363409260302345@g.us        │ General                 │\n│ 120363408822325057@g.us        │ openclaw_test           │\n│ 120363408212902124@g.us        │ test_group              │\n└────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n4 groups returned from `groupFetchAllParticipating()`. WhatsApp phone app shows 3 groups — `openclaw_test` (Community), `General`, `test_group`. The API returns 4 entries because `openclaw_test` is a WhatsApp Community which Baileys represents as two separate group JIDs (announcement + sub-group). This is expected protocol-level behavior.\n\n> **🖼️ WhatsApp app shows 3 groups: `openclaw_test` (Community), `General`, `test_group`\n<img width=\"430\" height=\"954\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3461c1a-a26d-4656-9eed-99bdf4409e9b\" />\n\nWhat was not tested: Crabbox cross-platform proof.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "branch": "fix/issue-76722-whatsapp-directory-groups-live",
